kg:note_ref7836_scopecontent_1_p_0 a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdf:value "- SK-28 is the twenty-eighth of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on archaeological remains, reliefs and inscriptions, prehistoric artifacts and decorative motifs related to Babylon (Iraq), Baghdad (Iraq), Bujnurd (Iran), Constantinople (Turkey), Hamadan (Iran), Harsin (Iran), Isfahan (Iran), Masshad (Iran), Nihavand (Iran), Ray (Iran), Saveh (Iran) and the prehistoric mound of Tepe Giyan (Iran)." .

