        kg:concept_lcsh_sh85006507,
        kg:concept_lcsh_sh85112527 ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by kg:title_ref7599 ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300027182,
        kg:concept_aat_300027339,
        kg:concept_drawings,
        kg:concept_sketches ;
    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Sketchbooks, housed in document boxes and stored on shelves, are organized by Joseph Upton into 13 subject categories.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note \"The field activities of the Persepolis Expedition were initiated by Professor Ernst Herzfeld in Spring 1931, after the French archaeological monopoly had been replaced by the new Antiquity Law, which opened Iran to archaeological field work by other nations. The expedition ended in fall 1939, after the outbreak of World War II. [...] At the end of 1934, Herzfeld was removed from his position as expedition director. He left Persepolis for the last time toward the end of November 1934 and went to London.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.137 and P.161]",
        "Former Title or Title Variations Ernst Herzeld; Skizzenbuch XXI: Persepolis",
        "Funding note \"Herzfeld returned to Persepolis in 1931 as field director. The project was conducted under the auspices of the Oriental Institute at the University of Chicago, with additional financial assistance from other American individuals and institutions.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.146]",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Herzfeld's original sketchbook title and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; SK-21 FSA A.06 02.07.21",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 1 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Main Gate [(Gate of All Lands)]: measured drawings of [colossal sculpture depicting man-bull], [see FSA A.6 05.0856], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.0406; FSA A.6 04.GN.1584; FSA A.6 04.GN.2287; FSA A.6 04.GN.2288].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 10 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], excavation sounding No. 2: measured plan.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 12 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Apadana], [Audience Hall and East, West, and North Porticoes]: measured sketches of [campaniform] column bases, [see FSA A.6 05.0896], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2314; FSA A.6 04.GN.1624; FSA A.6 04.GN.1625; FSA A.6 04.GN.2315; FSA A.6 04.GN.2316; FSA A.6 04.GN.2317]; measured sketches of lion capital.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 13 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana, [West Portico]: sketches of column capital, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1621; FSA A.6 04.GN.2301].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 14 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana, [West Portico]: measured drawing of column capital, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1621; FSA A.6 04.GN.2301].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 17 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Throne Hall], Unfinished Gate: [sketch of the preliminary excavation and of the addorsed bull capital]; as well as [measured drawings of] column and capital.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 7 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [comparison of composite] capitals and bases of columns [from the Gate of All Lands, the Apadana and the Council Hall (Tripylon)].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 8 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], excavation sounding No. 2: measured plan.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 15 to 16 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana, [North Portico]: measured drawing of column capital, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1623].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 4 and 5 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Gate of All Lands]: measured drawings of standing columns of stone with composite capitals, [see FSA A.6 05.0848], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1582; FSA A.6 04.GN.2290; FSA A.6 04.GN.2291].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Skizzenbuch XXI: Persepolis.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - SK-21 is the twenty-first of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on topography, archaeological remains, architecture, artifacts and decorative motifs related to Istakhr (Iran) and Persepolis (Iran).",
        "Scope and Contents Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 2: Sketchbooks; Subseries 2.07: Persepolis: Sketchbook 21" ;
