    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Sketchbooks, housed in document boxes and stored on shelves, are organized by Joseph Upton into 13 subject categories.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note \"Ernst Herzfeld's years in Iran [Persia] from [February] 1923 to [the end of October] 1925 were made possible by a private company with limited liability called the Gesellschaft zur Förderung von Ausgrabungen und Forschungsreisen GmbH, which was founded in 1923. Its aim was to foster excavations and scientific expeditions in Asia and to publish the results. [...]. [Consequently] Herzfeld was able to travel freely in Iran and survey most major archaeological sites.\" [Jens Kröger, \"Ernst Herzfeld and Friedrich Sarre\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.61 and P.64]",
        "Former Title or Title Variations Ernst Herzeld; Skizzenbuch XIII: Persien, Sistan-Quhistan, 1925",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Herzfeld's original sketchbook title and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; SK-13 FSA A.06 02.04.13",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 1 reads, \"Peshawar Museum: [Arabic] inscription of 483 H..\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 10 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: [section plan of Palace-Temple complex including South Gate, [see FSA A.6 05.0339].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 11 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: elevation and measured details of decorative molding, decorative niche, and arcades (in corner of courtyard), [see FSA A.6 05.0351; FSA A.6 05.0352; FSA A.6 05.0353].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 12 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: left) Palace-Temple complex, North Terrace: elevation reminiscent of Aiwan i Karkh [section of upper vaulted chamber], [see FSA A.6 05.0337; FSA A.6 05.0337a]; right) [decorative molding] above paintings in [Painted] Gallery.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 13 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of fortified structure called Kok-e Zal]: elevation of doorway and plan of section of fort with round tower, [see FSA A.6 05.0691; FSA A.6 05.0691a].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 2 reads, \"[(Mumbai (India)], Bombay Museum: [Arabic] inscription, in Kufic script, on sarcophagus, 410 H., [see FSA A.6 05.0760].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 25 reads, \"Zahedan [(Iran)]: tomb inscription, 850 H., [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2876].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 26 reads, \"[vicinity of Zahedan (Iran), Minaret at Qasimabad]: [Arabic] inscription (lower) [made of molded baked bricks], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2871; FSA A.6 04.GN.2872; FSA A.6 04.GN.2873].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 27 reads, \"[vicinity of Zahedan (Iran), Minaret at Qasimabad]: [Arabic] inscription (upper) [made of molded baked bricks], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2869; FSA A.6 04.GN.2870].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 28 reads, \"Kelat-i Abazar [(Iran)], plan of main section [of fortress]; [see FSA A.6 05.0391].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 3 reads, \"Notes on maps of Sistan [(Iran)], [see FSA A.6 05.0355].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 30 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: great gate inscription and notes on dating, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2894; FSA A.6 04.GN.2901].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 31 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: top) measured plan of south side, [see FSA A.6 05.0713]; bottom) color notes on tiles.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 32 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: masters' inscriptions, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2895].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 38 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: measured plans of sections, [see FSA A.6 05.1387]; section of inscription and Kufic monograms.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 39 reads, \"Khargird (Iran), madrasa al-Nizamiyya: mihrab floral designs, [see FSA A.6 05.0153], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2971; FSA A.6 04.GN.2972; FSA A.6 04.GN.2973].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 4 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: [sketch plan (section) of Palace-Temple complex including east iwan, [see FSA A.6 05.0338].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 40 reads, \"vicinity of Ribat i Safid [(Iran)], Kale i dukhtar [(Qal'a-ye Dokhtar)] (and Kale i pisar): plan and notes [of the Sasanian fortress], [see FSA A.6 05.0722], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1754].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 41 reads, \"Radkan (Iran), tomb tower at Radkan, East: [brick ornamentation and encircling band of Arabic inscription, in Kufic script], [see FSA A.6 05.0762], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2959; FSA A.6 04.GN.2960; FSA A.6 04.GN.2735; FSA A.6 04.GN.2738; FSA A.6 04.GN.2961].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 42 reads, \"Radkan (Iran), tomb tower at Radkan, East: plan, [see FSA A.6 05.0762]; and Tus [(Iran)]: tomb tower tambour.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 43 reads, \"Tus [(Iran)], Haruniya Mausoleum: plan, [see FSA A.6 05.0396]; and two [Arabic] inscriptions on gravestone, [see FSA A.6 06.A10; FSA A.6 06.A11b].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 46 reads, \"Sang Bast [(Iran)], Arslan Jadhib Mausoleum and Minaret: plan of tomb, [see FSA A.6 05.0395].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 48 reads, \"Notes on map of [southern] and [northern] Persia.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 5 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: [section plan of Palace-Temple complex including east iwan, [see FSA A.6 05.0338].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 8 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: [section plan of Palace-Temple complex including east iwan, [see FSA A.6 05.0338].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 9 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr]: [section plan of Palace-Temple complex including Painted Gallery under North Terrace].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 14 and 15 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], measured plans of fort, [see FSA A.6 05.0343].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 16 to 20 reads, \"Shahristan [(Iran)], [ruins of Qale-i Kuh]: topographical map of terrain and ruins, [see FSA A.6 05.0695; FSA A.6 05.0696; FSA A.6 05.0728; FSA A.6 05.0729; FSA A.6 05.0829].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 21 to 24 reads, \"Shahristan [(Iran)]: reconstruction of prehistoric pottery, profiles and patterns, [see FSA A.6 05.0661; FSA A.6 05.0662].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 28 and 29 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: measured plan, west side, [see FSA A.6 05.0713].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 32 and 33 reads, \"Khargird [(Iran)], madrasa al-Ghiyasiyya: measured plan, east side and outside, [see FSA A.6 05.0713].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 34 and 35 reads, \"Khargird (Iran), madrasa al-Nizamiyya: [Arabic inscription of Nizam al-Mulk, in tall Kufic script with floriated stems], [see FSA A.6 05.0363], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2736; FSA A.6 04.GN.2952; FSA A.6 04.GN.2955; FSA A.6 04.GN.2957; FSA A.6 04.GN.2970].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 36 and 37 reads, \"Khargird (Iran), madrasa al-Nizamiyya: measured plan of main iwan, [see FSA A.6 05.0403; FSA A.6 05.0404; FSA A.6 05.0711], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2975; FSA A.6 04.GN.2976; FSA A.6 04.GN.2977].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 44 and 45 reads, \"Tus [(Iran)], Haruniya Mausoleum: plan of ground and upper storeys, [see FSA A.6 05.0396]; and plan of mud brick building.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 6 to 7 reads, \"Kuh-e Khwaja [(Iran)], [ruins of Ghaga-Shahr, Palace-Temple complex, North Terrace]: measured plans, [see FSA A.6 05.0692; FSA A.6 05.0693; FSA A.6 05.0727].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Skizzenbuch XIII: Persien, Sistan-Quhistan, 1925\"",
        "Scope and Contents - SK-13 is the thirteenth of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on topography, landscape, inscriptions and reliefs, archaeological remains, architecture, artifacts and decorative motifs related to Kuh-e Khwaja (Iran), Shahristan (Iran), Zahedan (Iran), Qasimabad (Iran), Khargird (Iran), Mil-i Radkan (Iran), Tus (Iran), and Sangbast (Iran).",
        "Scope and Contents Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 2: Sketchbooks; Subseries 2.04: Persia, Sistan-Quhistan, 1925: Sketchbook 13" ;
