    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Sketchbooks, housed in document boxes and stored on shelves, are organized by Joseph Upton into 13 subject categories.",
        "Former Title or Title Variations Ernst Herzeld; Skizzenbuch XXV: A",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Herzfeld's original sketchbook title and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; SK-25 FSA A.06 02.10.25",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 1 reads, \"Nineveh [(ancient city, Iraq)], [fragments of] prehistoric pottery [with painted pattern and animal design]; [references to Campbell Thompson's excavation at Nineveh]; [London], [2 September 1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 13 reads, \"[Ur (Iraq)], two animal figurines made of clay.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 17 reads, \"stone objects from Ur; [3.09.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 19 reads, \"stone [object depicting] a frog and bronze pick-axe, in British Museum; [3.09.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 2 reads, \"bibliographical references [related to Campbell Thompson's excavation at Nineveh].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 23 reads, \"sling stone and spindle whorl, from Nineveh [(Iraq)]; two ceramic vessels (Al-Ubaid type) with painted pattern, from Ur [(Iraq)]; [4.IX.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 25 reads, \"animal head like early Sumerian.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 27 reads, \"Khinaman [(Iran)], four bronze [(copper alloy)] vessels [(bowl and spouted bowl)] in British Museum.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 29 reads, \"Khinaman [(Iran)], socketed copper ceremonial axe-head, in British Museum.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 3 reads, \"Nineveh [(Iraq)], [Campbell Thompson's excavation], cylinder seal from the [Kassite period].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 31 reads, \"Hamadan [(Iran)], bronze ceremonial axe-head, in British Museum.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 32 reads, \"unidentified alabaster vessel.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 33 reads, \"alabastron [vessel], [SAM 65], from Samarra [(Iraq)], [see FSA A.6 07.31.24].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 4 reads, \"bibliographical references.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 45 reads, \"Samarra [(Iraq)], [profiles of prehistoric pottery], [SAM 199].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 47 reads, \"[Samarra (Iraq)], [fragments of prehistoric pottery], [SAM 67] and [SAM 66].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 49 reads, \"thick glass vessel, from Samarra [(Iraq)].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 5 reads, \"[Nineveh (Iraq)], [Campbell Thompson's excavation], two animal beads, c. 2500 B.C..\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 51 reads, \"[potters marks] on Samarra pottery, [SAM 267], [SAM 280], [SAM 325], [SAM 203], [SAM 204], [SAM 89], [SAM 326], [SAM 601], [SAM 58], [SAM 52], [SAM 53].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 53 reads, \"pottery jar [(prehistoric vessel)] [with painted pattern and potter's mark], from Samarra [(Iraq)], [see FSA A.6 07.31.24].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 55 reads, \"Clay [human figurine] (idol) in three pieces, from Samarra [(Iraq)], [see FSA A.6 07.31.24].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 57 reads, \"[Samarra [(Iraq)], two fragments of prehistoric vessels with painted pattern depicting demon without head].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 59 reads, \"Samarra objects in shist, [SAM 80], [SAM 166], [SAM 238].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 61 reads, \"[alabastron vessel], [SAM 512], from Samarra [(Iraq)], [see FSA A.6 07.31.24].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 63 reads, \"vial, painted clay, from Samarra [(Iraq)], [Sam 751].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 67 reads, \"Samarra [(Iraq)]: [Palace of the Caliph (Dar al-Khilafa, Jawsaq al-Khaqani, Bayt al-Khalifah): rim of a basin], [see FSA A.6 05.1035], [see FSA A.6 04.PF.22.027], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.3190; FSA A.6 04.GN.3197].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 69 reads, \" Iron dagger handle with human masks from Harsin [(Iran)].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 7 reads, \"Ur [(Iraq)], [four ceramic vessels (Al-Ubaid type) with painted pattern], [3.IX.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 9 reads, \"Ur [(Iraq)], [three ceramic vessels (Al-Ubaid type) with painted pattern], [3.IX.1930]..\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 10 and 11 reads, \"[Ur (Iraq)], two jar sealings: a) V 13607; b) V 13963.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 14 and 15 reads, \"three types of cylinder seals from Ur [(Iraq)]: [top) V 14962; center) V 13492; bottom) V 13703, V 13711]; [3.IX.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 20 and 21 reads, \"gold coin and Sasanian seal stones in British Museum; [3.09.1930].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 35, 37, and 39 reads, \"mussel shells, from Samarra [(Iraq)]: [SAM 46], [SAM 47], [SAM 50], [SAM 49], [SAM 62], [SAM 51], [SAM 48], [SAM 56], [SAM 58], [SAM 52], [SAM 53], [SAM 59], [SAM 57], [SAM 55], [SAM 60], [SAM 71], [SAM 54], [SAM 76], [SAM 73], [SAM 74], [SAM 78], [SAM 87], [SAM 170], [SAM 507], [SAM 77], [SAM 86].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 41 and 43 reads, \"Samarra [(Iraq)], [profiles of prehistoric pottery], [SAM 190] and [SAM 191].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 64 and 65 reads, \"Samarra [(Iraq)]:Marble rim, [see FSA A.6 05.1035], [see FSA A.6 04.PF.22.027], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.3190; FSA A.6 04.GN.3197].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 70 and 71 reads, \" Inscribed Sasanian sealings (Bullae) from Takht Abu Nasr (Shiraz), Dec. 25, 1933; and Kufic inscription from Kermanshah.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Skizzenbuch XXV: A.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - SK-25 is the twenty-fifth of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on archaeological remains, prehistoric artifacts and decorative motifs related to Nineveh (Iraq), Ur (Iraq), Samarra (Iraq), Hamadan (Iran), Harsin (Iran), Kermanshah (Iran), and Shiraz (Iran). The observations on objects from Nineveh, Ur, and Hamadan were made from artifacts in the British Museum. The sketches related to Samarra were made at the time of Herzfeld last visit to the site.",
        "Scope and Contents Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 2: Sketchbooks; Subseries 2.10: Prehistoric Objects: Sketchbook 25",
        "Scope and Contents note (unless noted, even pages are blank)" ;
