    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Sketchbooks, housed in document boxes and stored on shelves, are organized by Joseph Upton into 13 subject categories.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note \"The field activities of the Persepolis Expedition were initiated by Professor Ernst Herzfeld in Spring 1931, after the French archaeological monopoly had been replaced by the new Antiquity Law, which opened Iran to archaeological field work by other nations. The expedition ended in fall 1939, after the outbreak of World War II. [...] At the end of 1934, Herzfeld was removed from his position as expedition director. He left Persepolis for the last time toward the end of November 1934 and went to London.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.137 and P.161]",
        "Former Title or Title Variations Ernst Herzeld; Skizzenbuch XIX: Persepolis",
        "Funding note \"Herzfeld returned to Persepolis in 1931 as field director. The project was conducted under the auspices of the Oriental Institute at the University of Chicago, with additional financial assistance from other American individuals and institutions.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.146]",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Herzfeld's original sketchbook title and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; SK-19 FSA A.06 02.07.19",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 1 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [topographical] measurements for mountains on edge of plain: Kūh-i Nasare-Khanä, Kūh-i Sachl, Kūh-i Gerd.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 10 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: alabastron, bronze ring [with animal design], altar and column base.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 11 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Harem [of Xerxes]: [partial plan of west wing], [see FSA A.6 05.0866].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 12 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Harem [of Xerxes]: [partial plan on west side of main wing], [see FSA A.6 05.0865; FSA A.6 05.0866; FSA A.6 05.1238].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 13 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Harem [of Xerxes]: [partial plan of west wing] (continued), [see FSA A.6 05.0866].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 14 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [floor pavement] over graves (related to p.7).\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 15 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: plan of building [south-east corner], [see FSA A.6 05.0874] with location and drawing of finds.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 16 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Tripylon [Council Hall]: plan of [southern portico] and small staircase, [see FSA A.6 05.0842]; [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2347].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 17 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], plan of building north of Tripylon [Council Hall], [see FSA A.6 05.0842].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 18 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: stone plaque with lion and affronted sphinxes (location on p.15); east of TaĊara [Tachara (Palace of Darius)]: remains of jar.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 19 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Tripylon (Council Hall)]: plan, [see FSA A.6 05.0889].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 2 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], plan of summit of Kūh-I Sachl and of cistern.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 20 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: [plan of building southern half], [see FSA A.6 05.0874] with measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 21 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: [plan of building southern half], [see FSA A.6 05.0874] with measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 22 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Unfinished Gate: plan, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2295; FSA A.6 04.GN.2296].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 23 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 24 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], four stone fragments.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 25 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], excavation sounding No. 2 [(probably excavation sounding No. 3 according to FSA A.6 05.0833)]: measured plan with location of stone fragments, [see FSA A.6 05.0833].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 26 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], excavation sounding No. 5: plan and elevation.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 27 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], excavation sounding No. 2 [(probably excavation sounding No. 3 according to FSA A.6 05.0833)]: measured plan, [see FSA A.6 05.0833].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 28 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)]: left) excavation sounding No. 2 [(probably excavation sounding No. 3 according to FSA A.6 05.0833)]: plan and elevation, [see FSA A.6 05.0833]; right) excavation sounding No. 1: plan, [see FSA A.6 05.0834].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 29 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)]: left) excavation sounding No. 3: city wall, [see FSA A.6 05.0835]; right) excavation sounding No. 2 [(probably excavation sounding No. 3 according to FSA A.6 05.0833)]: plan.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 3 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], sketch elevations of Kūh-i Sachl and Kūh-i Nasare-Khanä; measurements for map of plain; [funerary inscriptions associated with] astodans (astudans) on Kūh-i Sachl.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 30 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Harem [of Xerxes], [main wing]: plan of [principal courtyard and northern portico], [see FSA A.6 05.0865; FSA A.6 05.0866; FSA A.6 05.0868; FSA A.6 05.1238].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 31 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Tripylon (Council Hall)]: plan of northern stairway, [see FSA A.6 05.0842].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 35 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)]: plan of small stairway, west of the main building], [see FSA A.6 05.0846].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 4 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], measurements for map of plain.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 44 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], location of \"goldnes Schmuckstab\".\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 45 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], prehistoric village, kiln.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 46 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], prehistoric village, kiln.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 47 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], location of \"Bronzebeschlag\".\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 48 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], measurements for map of Hajji Nasrullah water channel (qanāt) from Istakhr.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 5 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], course of Polvar [(Pulvar)] River across plain.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 6 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [perspective drawing of unidentified graves].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 7 reads, \"between Naqsh-i Rajab [(Iran)] and Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], [unidentified graves].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 8 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: plan of building [north-west corner with basis for a fire altar], [see FSA A.6 05.0873].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 9 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Fratadara Temple]: [plan of building northern half], [see FSA A.6 05.0873]; remains of Greek [votive] inscription.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Skizzenbuch XIX: Persepolis.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - SK-19 is the nineteenth of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on topography, landscape, inscriptions and reliefs, archaeological remains, architecture, artifacts and decorative motifs related to Istakhr (Iran), and Persepolis (Iran).",
        "Scope and Contents Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 2: Sketchbooks; Subseries 2.07: Persepolis: Sketchbook 19" ;
