    crm:P3_has_note "Arrangement Sketchbooks, housed in document boxes and stored on shelves, are organized by Joseph Upton into 13 subject categories.",
        "Date/Time and Place of an Event Note \"The field activities of the Persepolis Expedition were initiated by Professor Ernst Herzfeld in Spring 1931, after the French archaeological monopoly had been replaced by the new Antiquity Law, which opened Iran to archaeological field work by other nations. The expedition ended in fall 1939, after the outbreak of World War II. [...] At the end of 1934, Herzfeld was removed from his position as expedition director. He left Persepolis for the last time toward the end of November 1934 and went to London.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.137 and P.161]",
        "Former Title or Title Variations Ernst Herzeld; Skizzenbuch XVII: Persepolis",
        "Funding note \"Herzfeld returned to Persepolis in 1931 as field director. The project was conducted under the auspices of the Oriental Institute at the University of Chicago, with additional financial assistance from other American individuals and institutions.\" [Elspeth R. M. Dusinberre, \"Herzfeld in Persepolis\", Ernst Herzfeld and the Development of Near Eastern Studies, 1900-1950. Edited by Ann Gunter and Stefan R. Hauser. Leiden: Brill, 2005. P.146]",
        "General - Title is provided by Xavier Courouble, FSg Archives cataloger, based on Herzfeld's original sketchbook title and Joseph Upton's Catalogue of the Herzfeld Archive.",
        "Local Numbers Ernst Herzfeld Papers; SK-17 FSA A.06 02.07.17",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 1 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], measurements for beginning of Apadana drainage system.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 10 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], measurements for excavation sounding No. 2.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 12 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Tripylon [(Council Hall)]: elevation of stairway [before excavation].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 14 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], main gateway [Gate of All Lands], southern doorway: plan and elevation [including decorative stone ring of west socket stone].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 15 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], main gateway [Gate of All Lands], eastern doorway: plan and elevation [including decorative stone ring of west socket stone].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 16 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], main gateway [Gate of All Lands], western doorway: plan and elevation, [see FSA A.6 05.0848, FSA A.6 05.0882].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 17 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], main gateway [Gate of All Lands]: [stone] mason's mark and detail of volute, [see FSA A.6 05.1143, FSA A.6 05.1181].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 18 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], left) TaĊara [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)]: plan of south-east corner; right) Hadish (Palace of Xerxes): section of vestibule and plan of drainage system north of Hadish, [see FSA A.6 05.1471].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 19 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], section of column base.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 20 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana: drawings of canals in north section of great Hall [Audience Hall], [see FSA A.6 05.0849; FSA A.6 05.0877].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 21 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana: plan of drainage system in south-east corner.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 22 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Hadish [(Palace of Xerxes)]: column bases north of Hadish in front of small staircase [eastern stairway], [see FSA A.6 05.0884].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 23 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], drainage system north of TaĊara [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)], [see FSA A.6 05.0846; FSA A.6 05.0877].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 24 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana: drainage system in north-west section of hundred-column hall [Audience Hall], [see FSA A.6 05.0852; FSA A.6 05.0877].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 25 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Apadana]: drainage system in hundred-column hall [Audience Hall], [see FSA A.6 05.0877].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 26 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Throne Hall]: stairway to drainage system, east of hundred-column hall, [see FSA A.6 05.0877].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 27 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], foundation levels of Apadana and hundred-column Hall [(Throne Hall)].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 28 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], TaĊara [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)]: [design of] walking lion [on hem of King's gown in relief], [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1689, FSA A.6 04.GN.1690].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 29 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Apadana]: reconstruction of glazed-brick decoration with color notes, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.0335, FSA A.6 04.GN.0336; FSA A.6 04.GN.0337, FSA A.6 04.GN.0338].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 30 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], TaĊara [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)]: [design of] walking lion [on hem of King's gown in relief], on northern doorway, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.1689, FSA A.6 04.GN.1690].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 43 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], elevation of city wall, [see FSA A.6 05.0835].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 47 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Fratadara [Temple]: section of plan east of room five, [see FSA A.6 05.0873].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 48 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], [sacred precinct]: measurements for the enclosure wall.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 49 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)]: plan of the enclosure wall, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.2225].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 50 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], unidentified building.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 51 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], [sacred precinct]: more measurements for the enclosure wall.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 52 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Hadish (Palace of Xerxes), western stairway: measurements.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 53 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], east of TaĊara [Tachara Palace (Palace of Darius)]: plan and drainage system, [see FSA A.6 05.0846].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 54 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], [sacred precinct]: measurements for the enclosure wall.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 55 reads, \"Naqsh-i Rustam [(Iran)], [sacred precinct]: plan for the enclosure wall, [see FSA A.6 05.0779; FSA A.6 05.0795].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 56 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Tripylon [(Council Hall)], [courtyard south] of Tripylon: plan of small column bases, [see FSA A.6 05.0873].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 57 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], Apadana: [plan of rooms located on the north-east corner of the structure], [see FSA A.6 05.0849].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 6 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], measurements for plan; and for excavation sounding No. 3.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 7 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], elevation of city wall (30.11.[19]32), [see FSA A.6 05.0835].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 8 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], measurements for excavation sounding No. 4 and sketches of two column bases.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 85 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], drainage opening near great stairway.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 9 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)], sketch elevation and plan of excavation sounding No. 4.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 98 reads, \"Gerdek [(Turkey)], measurements for plotting of mound.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, caption for pg. 99 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], unexplained plan [possibly eastern wall of Terrace complex].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 100, 101, and 102 reads, \"Akhur-i Rustam [(Iran)], astudans [(astodans, rock-cut cavities)], [entrance door to the tomb as well as half-columns with impost-block depicting a pair of animal protomes].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 103 and 104 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Apadana]: reconstruction of glazed-brick decoration with color notes, [see FSA A.6 04.GN.0335, FSA A.6 04.GN.0336; FSA A.6 04.GN.0337, FSA A.6 04.GN.0338].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 31 to 41 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], measurements for plans of various structures and drainage system on terrace complex.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 44 and 45 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], [Office of the Guards on the north wall of Terrace complex]: [plan of the upper story], [see FSA A.6 05.0778; FSA A.6 05.0828].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 60 to 84 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)]and [Naqsh-i Rustam (Iran)], measurements for area plan, Nov.14, 1933.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 86, 87, to 88 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], graves (?) and [drainage system].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 89 to 95 reads, \"Istakhr [(Iran)]: fragments of Achaemenian column, re-used in a Medieval mosque, [see FSA A.6 05.0732; FSA A.6 05.1167; FSA A.6 05.1168; FSA A.6 05.1169].\"",
        "Scope and Contents - In Finding Aid, captions for pg. 96 and 97 reads, \"Persepolis [(Iran)], graves on moutain to north.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - Original handwritten title on cover reads: \"Ernst Herzfeld; Skizzenbuch XVII: Persepolis.\"",
        "Scope and Contents - SK-17 is the seventeenth of a series of thirty-five sketchbooks (Skizzenbücher), in which Ernst Herzfeld recorded his observations on topography, landscape, reliefs, archaeological remains, architecture, and decorative motifs related to Istakhr (Iran), Naqsh-i Rustam (Iran), and Persepolis (Iran).",
        "Scope and Contents Ernst Herzfeld Papers, Series 2: Sketchbooks; Subseries 2.07: Persepolis: Sketchbook 17" ;
